This licence covers the build and app code in this repository: build.sh,
check.sh, index.html (template and app logic), and tools/*.py. It does not
cover the engine/ submodule, which is a separate repository (vocab-engine)
with its own MIT licence, or the pack data described below.

## Pack data

The data under `pack/` (words, sentences, and the generated sentences in
`tools/*.tsv`) is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
4.0 International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

This reflects upstream share-alike terms: glosses, part of speech and kana
readings come from Wiktionary via kaikki.org (CC BY-SA 3.0 / GFDL), and
general frequency data comes from the `wordfreq` package (CC BY-SA 4.0),
both of which require share-alike redistribution of derived data.

Example sentences, translations, word-index links and furigana are from
Tatoeba (CC BY 2.0 FR) and remain attributed by contributor in
`pack/attribution.json`.

Build-time tools used to construct this pack (SudachiPy + SudachiDict-core,
Apache-2.0; MeCab + ipadic, used only by `wordfreq` for tokenising) are used
only while building the pack and ship nothing into the built output. They do
not affect the licence of the shipped code or pack data. See the "Sources
and licences" table in README.md for the full list of sources used per data
type.
